       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The maximum for ibuprofen in adults is 3,200 mg/day under supervision. The OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n\nA dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCommon regimens that may be what you meant:\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions.\n- **400\u2013800 mg by mouth, 3 times daily** for pain or inflammation.\n- **1600 mg total per day**, for example 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it. If 1600 mg four times daily is intentional, please confirm that. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first, and I can add a note to the order if you'd like."
